            "kind": "relative",
            "params": {
              "anchor_text": "User ID",
              "relation": "same_row",
              "role": "textbox"
            },
            "rationale": "the 'User ID' table row has exactly one control; row-scoping is needed because this bare <input> has no accessible name of its own for get_by_role(name=...) to match -- no <label>, no aria-label, just a sibling <td> the accessibility tree does not associate with it"
          },
          {
            "kind": "structural",
            "params": {
              "path": "input[name=uid]"
            },
            "rationale": "the field's HTML name attribute is stable legacy-app plumbing, unlikely to change even if the visible label wording does"
